Cadence — a todo app on **Next.js 16.3.5 (App Router, Turbopack) + React 19 +
Tailwind v4 + zod v4**, TypeScript strict. Pure frontend: no API routes, no
database, no server-side logic at all. The **browser calls the `demo-backend`
Todo API directly** over an httpOnly session cookie.

## The architecture, in one picture

```
browser ──────────────────► demo-backend :5000     ← every /api/* call
   │
   └── Next.js :3000 serves HTML, JS and CSS. That is all it does.
```

There is no `browser → Next.js → API` hop. No Server Actions, no route handlers,
no server-side session. Consequences you cannot design around: this server never
receives the session cookie, so it cannot render user data; CORS and
`credentials: "include"` are load-bearing; and there is no server cache to
revalidate.

Assume Next 16 differs from what you remember. `middleware` is now `proxy` (not
used here), `cookies()`/`params`/`searchParams` are async-only, `next lint` is
gone. See `docs/next-16.md` before using a framework API.

## Commands
`npm run dev` (:3000, backend on :5000) · `npm run build` · `npm run lint`
(`lint:fix`) · `npm run format` (`format:check`, prettier) · `npx tsc --noEmit`.
No test suite. `.env` needs `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL`; the server exits at
start-up if it is missing. The backend needs `CORS_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000`.

## Always
1. **No `fetch` outside `lib/api/`** — ESLint enforces it. Use `apiRequest` /
   `apiData` / `apiList`.
2. **Authorization belongs to the API.** `useRequireSession()` only redirects the
   UI; it protects nothing. Never treat a client-side check as a boundary.
3. **No hard-coded colours** — semantic utilities only (`bg-surface`,
   `text-ink-muted`, `border-hairline`). Tokens: `app/globals.css`.
4. **Branch on `ApiError.code`, never `.message`.**
5. **Server Components by default**; `"use client"` for state, effects, handlers
   — and for anything touching the API. Keep the boundary low in the tree.
6. Match the surrounding file's comment density — this codebase explains *why*,
   not *what*. Don't add narration to code that doesn't have it.

